<h3>Walkabout Magazine</h3>
<p><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walkabout_(magazine)">Walkabout Magazine</a> was Australia's premier travel and geography monthly from 1934, a publication that took seriously the proposition that Australians should know their own continent before looking elsewhere. Keith contributed between 1962 and 1969, filing long-form pieces from regional towns, outback stations and coastal cities that rarely made the metropolitan press — portraits of a country still in the process of understanding its own scale and diversity. The magazine's combination of lavish photography and literary reportage gave Keith room to write at a length and pace that daily journalism never allowed, and several of his best pieces from this period read as miniature books in their own right.</p>
