<h3>Reader's Digest</h3>
<p>The Australian edition of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reader%27s_Digest">Reader's Digest</a> was, through the 1960s and 1970s, one of the most widely read magazines in the country — a publication that reached households well beyond the capital-city readership of the dailies and weeklies. Keith contributed several pieces during the 1970s, writing in a register more expansive than his newspaper columns allowed: the articles tend toward the reflective and the panoramic, taking subjects like the Melbourne-versus-Sydney rivalry or the peculiarities of an Australian Christmas and treating them as windows into something larger about how Australians understood themselves. The Digest's enormous circulation meant these pieces were read by more Australians than almost anything else he published.</p>
